Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:41:26 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Input: wacom_w9000: harden W9019 state transitions

Require an active-high flash-mode line for W9019. Acquire it without
driving malformed active-low descriptions and then hold the physical line
low for normal operation.

Make regulator and IRQ state independent and idempotent. A failed system
suspend restores reset and IRQ operation. A failed input close remains
quiesced and is repaired without adding a regulator vote on reopen. A
failed enable leaves both state flags off. Use shared production and KUnit
callback seams for fault injection.

Make query retry count and pacing variant data. W9019 uses the three
attempts and 100 ms inter-attempt delay in its public GPL implementation.
Existing variants retain combined transfers and eight unpaced attempts.

Preserve the existing input event sequence. Add query, event, and power
transition tests through the production seams.

The W9019 retry count and pacing come from the same Samsung GPL-2.0
driver: COM_QUERY_RETRY and wacom_i2c_query() in
drivers/input/wacom_tab/.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
